# Required. Connection string for the arald_portal Postgres database on Neon
# (docs/emergency-portal.md) — the same one arald-backend/sync.ts writes to.
# Never commit the real value; on Vercel, set it under Project Settings ->
# Environment Variables instead.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host/arald_portal?sslmode=require

# Required. Signing secret for Auth.js session JWTs (auth.ts) — generate one
# with `npx auth secret` or `openssl rand -base64 33`. Never commit the real
# value; on Vercel, set it under Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
# Rotating it invalidates every existing operator session.
AUTH_SECRET=change-me

# Required for the canale di comando (Pezzo 1, docs/emergency-portal.md).
# Encrypts each operator's dedicated mesh Ed25519 private key at rest
# (users.mesh_private_key_encrypted) — deliberately a SEPARATE secret from
# AUTH_SECRET (key separation: a leaked AUTH_SECRET lets an attacker forge
# portal sessions, a leaked value here lets one decrypt custodied mesh
# signing keys — two different blast radii, never the same secret).
# Generate with `openssl rand -hex 32` (exactly 32 raw bytes, hex-encoded —
# lib/mesh-key-encryption.ts rejects anything else). Never commit the real
# value; on Vercel, set it under Project Settings -> Environment Variables.
# Rotating it makes every already-stored operator private key undecryptable
# — there is no re-encryption tool (out of scope for this piece); a rotated
# key means every operator's mesh identity must be regenerated (a new
# identity, still recognized automatically the next time they submit a
# command — it just changes which node id the mesh sees).
MESH_IDENTITY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=change-me-32-bytes-hex
